# {{.Name}}

A Neutron Julia project. `{{.SDK.Name}}` is a **database client** for Nucleus (or
any PostgreSQL) — all data models over pgwire. There is no HTTP server in the
Julia SDK, so this project has no `/health` endpoint and `neutron dev` runs a
script rather than a server.

## Getting started

```sh
{{range .NextSteps}}{{.}}
{{end}}```

`neutron dev` runs `julia --project=. src/main.jl`, which connects to
`NEUTRON_DATABASE_URL` (default `postgres://localhost:5432/{{.Name}}`), runs
`SELECT 1` and reports whether the server is Nucleus.

`{{.SDK.Name}}` is not in the General registry. `Project.toml` points at the
Neutron repository through `[sources]`, which Julia 1.11+ reads during
`Pkg.instantiate()`. On older Julia, add it by URL instead:

```julia
using Pkg
Pkg.add(url="{{.SDK.Source}}", subdir="{{.SDK.Subdir}}")
```
